  "notes": "Detected by serial: digits 5-8 read 2017, which the kext's serial table (UAD2System.kext 12.0.0) maps to internal type 0x22, and CPcieDevice::Name() names 0x22 'Apollo x8p - HEXA'. The driver's older tables called 0x22 an x8 and 0x20 an x8p, which is why this unit used to be pinned by PCI subsystem ID 0x0014; the subsystem ID is now only a fallback when the serial lookup fails. Observed serial '2008 2017 00xxxx': serial_prefix is the model group at digits 5-8, serial_leading is digits 1-4. Audio confirmed on real hardware (issue #46): SG table programmed, SAMPLE_POS/FRAME_CTR advancing, audible playback via PipeWire, no DMAR faults with intel_iommu=on. Required 6016d4e (reset strobe re-clear) + 2df18d5 (SG table on ring-connect devices). Verified since (issue #52): all 8 preamps discrete over ALSA (-144..+65 dB, independent input select), channel identity 1:1 (physical input N -> capture AUX(N-1)), and 26/26 @ 48k full duplex stable over a 60s soak. d2d10bb raised the legacy DMA counts to 34 play / 32 rec (the ADAT-mode route counts) and a 32-channel capture ran clean on hardware. The device-read IO descriptor lists 34 inputs and 52 outputs; io_map=1 maps ALSA channels onto those slots by channel ID. Inputs 1-2 are front-panel Hi-Z; 3-8 are rear combo, mic/line only, defaulting to Mic. Control map is device_map_apollo_x8p.json (PR #54). Still unverified: rates other than 48k, digital I/O and clock. Tracked in issue #52.",
